permissions-invalid = Invalid permission change
permissions-changed = Files or the selected range changed. Refresh and review again.
permissions-verify-failed = Cannot verify the resulting permissions or ownership
permissions-preview = Review { $files } files and { $directories } directories before applying:
permissions-confirm = Apply changes
permissions-cancel = Cancel
permissions-acl = Additional access rules exist. Changing group permissions also changes the limit for those rules.
permissions-default-acl = This directory has default access rules inherited by newly created items; this form does not change them.
permissions-hardlinks = Other hard links to this file are affected too.
permissions-special-cleared = Changing ownership may clear special permissions or file capabilities. They are not restored automatically.
permissions-special-were-cleared = Linux cleared special permissions or file capabilities when ownership changed.
